// ============================================================================
// round-robin-games.epher -- league fixtures: ncr(n, 2) games
//
// In a round-robin league every pair of teams meets exactly once, and a
// pair of teams is an unordered set, so n teams play ncr(n, 2) games.
// With a home and an away leg the pair is ordered (team A hosts team B
// is a different fixture from B hosting A), which doubles the count to
// 2 * ncr(n, 2) = npr(n, 2).
//
// Cross-checks: npr(n, 2) = n * (n - 1) counts the ordered pairs
// directly, and 2 * ncr(n, 2) = npr(n, 2) verifies the doubling. All
// counts are exact integers.
//
// Source: standard combinatorics, as in Ross, "A First Course in
// Probability", chapter 1.
//
// Run it from a terminal:  epher "epher scripts/probability/counting/round-robin-games.epher"
// Web/desktop:             paste the file into the entry, press Enter
//
// The knob to edit is `teams`; everything below it is machinery.
// ============================================================================

// ---- the knob ----
const teams = 8

// ---- results ----
// One game per pair of teams.
print("single round robin,", teams, "teams:", ncr(teams, 2))
print("home and away:", 2 * ncr(teams, 2))

// The ordered view: n * (n - 1) fixtures with a designated home side.
2 * ncr(teams, 2) == npr(teams, 2)
print("ordered fixtures npr(8, 2):", npr(teams, 2))

// Other league sizes for the same formulas.
print("10 teams:", ncr(10, 2), "games,", 2 * ncr(10, 2), "with home and away")
print("12 teams:", ncr(12, 2), "games,", 2 * ncr(12, 2), "with home and away")

// A four-group world cup style stage: 4 groups of 4 teams, each group a
// mini round robin.
print("4 groups of 4 (group stage):", 4 * ncr(4, 2), "matches")

// A triangular check: an 8-team league with 28 games is the same count
// as the handshakes in a room of 8 people, and the polygon version of
// the same pair count: sides plus diagonals of an 8-sided figure.
print("handshakes in a room of", teams, "people:", ncr(teams, 2))
print("diagonals of an", teams, "-sided polygon:", ncr(teams, 2) - teams)
// ---- expected output ----
// = 8
// = single round robin, 8 teams: 28
// = home and away: 56
// = true
// = ordered fixtures npr(8, 2): 56
// = 10 teams: 45 games, 90 with home and away
// = 12 teams: 66 games, 132 with home and away
// = 4 groups of 4 (group stage): 24 matches
// = handshakes in a room of 8 people: 28
// = diagonals of an 8 -sided polygon: 20
